WEBVTT

00:01.062 --> 00:04.925
What if a laboratory could develop the
capabilities its next experiment

00:04.925 --> 00:05.600
needs?

00:05.925 --> 00:10.450
From digital equipment models to real
laboratory actions, this is the idea

00:10.450 --> 00:12.662
behind self-building laboratories.

00:20.588 --> 00:23.713
Self-driving laboratories automate
experiments.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.175
A self-building laboratory also develops
the capabilities those experiments

00:28.175 --> 00:28.812
require.

00:29.088 --> 00:31.338
A scientific goal reveals a gap.

00:31.638 --> 00:35.425
The system builds, validates, and retains
the missing capability.

00:36.538 --> 00:40.812
Photographs, equipment information, and
design files provide the starting

00:40.812 --> 00:41.400
point.

00:41.675 --> 00:44.500
Models describe moving parts and their
limits.

00:44.775 --> 00:48.812
Real observations help refine equipment
positions in the digital twin.

00:50.488 --> 00:53.025
Candidate motions are checked for
collisions.

00:53.300 --> 00:57.138
The agent develops control interfaces and
executable procedures.

00:57.400 --> 01:02.375
Near a fixture, visual and force feedback
refine alignment and insertion.

01:02.662 --> 01:07.325
Procedures become reusable skills, with
operating conditions, recovery

01:07.325 --> 01:09.525
steps, and runtime guardrails.

01:11.688 --> 01:15.762
We applied this process to cadmium sulfide
quantum-dot synthesis.

01:16.038 --> 01:19.975
An Opentrons liquid handler prepared a
ninety-six-well plate.

01:20.288 --> 01:22.950
A rail-mounted arm transferred it to a
sealer,

01:31.288 --> 01:33.587
changed its grasp at an intermediate
holder,

01:35.212 --> 01:37.038
and loaded an optical reader.

01:37.375 --> 01:41.438
The workflow combined two hundred and
thirty-six liquid-handler commands

01:41.438 --> 01:43.487
with nineteen robotic stages.

01:44.688 --> 01:48.375
The plate sampled different reagent ratios
and pH conditions.

01:48.688 --> 01:52.512
Optical measurements tracked fluorescence
development over eight hours.

01:52.812 --> 01:57.162
Capability development led to a physical
experimental workflow and a

01:57.162 --> 01:58.450
scientific measurement.

02:02.575 --> 02:07.000
In simulation, we also explored
coordinated workflows across different

02:07.000 --> 02:09.237
robots and multiple workstations.

02:09.525 --> 02:13.838
The aim is a laboratory that adapts as
scientific requirements change.

02:14.088 --> 02:17.288
Each validated skill expands what it can
do next.
